        "furry13"
      ],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "This attempts to address the comments received during IETF 125. It breaks out CLAP/PLAT, 2 options for \"existing behavior\", add packet behavior.\r\n\r\n**NOTE**: There are 2 options for \"existing behavior\" - please choose one.\r\n\r\nComments:\r\n* Momoka: Requested clarification on the current behavior of CLATs -  some implementations do not enforce the restriction discussed in the draft\r\n  * Section 4.1 expanded to highlight this, and this doc as the solution.\r\n\r\n* Nick: Agreed that instructions because inconsistent CLAT behavior. Suggested adding examples (perhaps remove before pub.)\r\n  *  Added Appendix, clarify Existing Behavior.\r\n  \r\n* Med: Provided feedback on the mailing list (referenced by Jen during presentation) on finding wording that does not break existing deployments while still allowing the Well-Known Prefix.\r\n  * Section 3 normative text was refined to distinguish between unmanaged CLATs (which MUST translate) and managed PLATs (which MAY drop by default to preserve existing security postures).  ",
      "createdAt": "2026-04-27T23:02:32Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-16T09:06:45Z",
