      "body": "- Fixing the title\r\n- Adding RFC6598 as a Normative, and sort the RFC numbers\r\n- Removing 'NAT64' from the 1st paragraph in the Intro and rephrasing the text to indicate we are talking about IPv4/IPv6 translators\r\n- Mentioning 64:ff9b:1::/48, [RFC8215] in the Intro, saying it's basically equal to the NSP\r\n- rephrasing the Intro text to make it explicit that we are only suggesting to allow the private addresses (RFC1918 etc), not ALL special addresses \r\n- I'm as confused as Nick is by the first paragraph in the Operational Considerations. Removing some text as I'm not convinced it's relevant\r\n- Rephrasing the NSP section of the Operational consoidertations to cover both NSP and 64:ff9b:1::/48 (which is not, strictly speaking, NSP) - and updating the section title\r\n- Updating the Ack section to keep names in the alphabetical order.",
